      "raw_output": "<think>\nThe room is a compact 6x5m apartment with a bed, sofa, table, chairs, kitchen elements, bath fixtures, and three storage units. The user wants to keep the existing cabinet arrangement but address potential window access and storage proximity issues. The storage units currently sit near the south side: A at (-1.67, -1.83), B at (-0.27, -1.69), and C at (-2.27, 0.37). Their original positions may crowd the circulation path between the bed and the south side, and C is close to the west wall. Moving them to the north side will create a clearer central zone and improve access to the bed and other furnishings. I will place A at (-1.4, 1.58) near the north wall, B at (0.9, 1.42) to the right, and C at (1.5, 1.1) more toward the center of the north side. This should give each unit breathing room while maintaining a continuous north-side storage band. I'll move all three now with the move_furniture_tool.\n</tool_call>\n<tool_call>{\"name\":\"move_furniture_tool\",\"arguments\": {\"object_id\": \"recon_storage_a_0\", \"x\": -1.4, \"y\": 1.58, \"yaw\": 0}}\n</tool_call>",
